🚽 Test case: #193 -- copy-initializing a by-value struct from a struct
🚽 POINTER variable (`gang Point c = pp;` with `gang Point *pp`) is a type
🚽 error, not an implicit dereference (PR #253 review, finding 1).
gang Point {
    rizz x;
};

skibidi main {
    gang Point q;
    q.x = 5;
    gang Point *pp = &q;
    gang Point c = pp;
    bussin 0;
}
